From: njq8 <318205820+njq8x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:18:01 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Run Netty login completion and disconnects on the main thread

The Netty stack ran two pieces of world-mutating code on event loop
threads:

* NetworkManagerHandler.channelInactive/exceptionCaught went straight
  into the disconnect path, which removes the player from the world, the
  entity tracker and the chunk watchers and queues its chunks for
  unloading.
* NetLoginHandler.b finished the login inside the future returned by
  getChunkAtAsync, that is, on an async chunk I/O thread, adding the
  player to the world and starting its chunk send queue.

Both touch main-thread-only state. In particular, the chunk unload queue
is a plain fastutil Long2LongOpenHashMap that is iterated while chunks
are unloaded: a concurrent put from an event loop thread corrupted the
iterator and threw IndexOutOfBoundsException out of
ChunkProviderServer.unloadChunks, which killed the server tick loop and
made every following login time out.

Post both continuations through MinecraftServer.queueTask, and skip the
login completion if the client is already gone.

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/canyonmodded/network/NetworkManagerHandler.java b/src/main/java/com/canyonmodded/network/NetworkManagerHandler.java
index 25d4811be..50848d113 100644
--- a/src/main/java/com/canyonmodded/network/NetworkManagerHandler.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/canyonmodded/network/NetworkManagerHandler.java
@@ -41,7 +41,11 @@ public class NetworkManagerHandler extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet> {
 
     @Override
     public void channelInactive(ChannelHandlerContext ctx) throws Exception {
-        networkManager.a("disconnect.closed");
+        // Disconnecting removes the player from the world, the entity tracker and
+        // the chunk watchers, and queues chunks for unloading. All of that is
+        // main-thread state, so it must not run on the event loop: doing so
+        // corrupted the chunk unload queue and killed the tick loop.
+        this.server.queueTask(() -> this.networkManager.a("disconnect.closed"));
     }
 
     @Override
@@ -51,10 +55,12 @@ public class NetworkManagerHandler extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet> {
 
     @Override
     public void exceptionCaught(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, Throwable cause) throws Exception {
-        if (cause instanceof ReadTimeoutException) {
-            networkManager.a("disconnect.timeout");
-        } else if (!(cause instanceof ClosedChannelException)) {
-            networkManager.a(cause);
-        }
+        this.server.queueTask(() -> {
+            if (cause instanceof ReadTimeoutException) {
+                this.networkManager.a("disconnect.timeout");
+            } else if (!(cause instanceof ClosedChannelException)) {
+                this.networkManager.a(cause);
+            }
+        });
     }
 }
